{
  type: install
  message: <<EOM
The Epithet services are disabled by default. Configure flat TOML files in
/usr/local/etc/epithet, install the referenced policy and static data files,
and generate distinct CA and control signing keys before enabling services.

Use epithet_server with server.toml for combined operation. For standalone
operation, use epithet_ca, epithet_control, epithet_directory, and
epithet_inventory with their corresponding ca.toml, control.toml,
directory.toml, and inventory.toml files. Do not enable both modes together.

The service account must be able to read both private keys:

  chown root:epithet /usr/local/etc/epithet/ca.key /usr/local/etc/epithet/control.key
  chmod 0640 /usr/local/etc/epithet/ca.key /usr/local/etc/epithet/control.key

Standalone directory and inventory services also need readable ca.key.pub
and control.key.pub. Configure the same OIDC settings in CA and control,
and advertise the public management URL with control-public in ca.toml.

Startup prepares directory/ and inventory/ under /var/db/epithet as needed
for the service account. If you change state-dir, prepare those subdirectories
with service-account ownership and mode 0700 yourself.
EOM
}
]
